{"theorems":[{"slogan_id":4371172,"theorem_id":19685900,"name":"Theorem \\normalsize 2.5","body":"\\textup{\\cite{M}} If graph $G$ with $|V_G|=n$ and $|E_G|=m$. The number of spanning trees of $G$ is\\begin{eqnarray*}  2m\\tau (G)=\\prod _{i=1}^{n}d_i\\cdot \\prod _{i=2}^{n}\\lambda _i, \\end{eqnarray*}where $\\lambda _{i}$ is the normalized Laplacian eigenvalue of $G$.","slogan":"A graph with n vertices and m edges has a spanning tree count given by a formula. This formula equals the product of all vertex degrees multiplied by the product of all normalized Laplacian eigenvalues except the smallest. The result is also equal to twice the number of edges times the number of spanning trees. The eigenvalues are those of the normalized Laplacian matrix of the graph.","theorem_type":"theorem","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"2009.04139v1","source":"arXiv","title":"The Laplacian and normalized Laplacian spectra of Mobius polyomino networks and their applications","authors":["Zhi-Yu Shi","Jia-Bao Liu","Sakander Hayat"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2009.04139v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.SP","categories":["math.SP"],"citations":0,"year":2020,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.7617694962552043,"score":0.7617694962552043,"has_metadata":true},{"slogan_id":2245310,"theorem_id":18276974,"name":"Theorem 5","body":"{\\cite{Chu97}} The total count of spanning trees of the graph $G$ is,\\begin{eqnarray*}  \\tau (G)=\\frac{1}{2|E|}\\prod \\limits _{i=1}^{|V|} d_i \\prod \\limits _{i=2}^{|V|} \\lambdabar _i, \\end{eqnarray*}where $\\{ 0=\\lambdabar _1< \\lambdabar _2\\leq \\cdots \\leq \\lambdabar _{|V|}\\} $ is the spectrum of the normalized Laplacian matrix of the graph $G$.","slogan":"The total number of spanning trees in a graph G is given by a formula involving the degrees of its vertices and the eigenvalues of its normalized Laplacian matrix. The product of all vertex degrees is multiplied by the product of all nonzero eigenvalues. This result is then divided by twice the number of edges in the graph. The eigenvalues are ordered, with the smallest being zero and excluded from the product.","theorem_type":"theorem","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"2302.07170v2","source":"arXiv","title":"Characterizing the Degree-Kirchhoff, Gutman, and Schultz Indices in Pentagonal Cylinders and Möbius Chains","authors":["Md. Abdus Sahir","Sk. Md. Abu Nayeem"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2302.07170v2","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.CO","categories":["math.CO","cs.DM"],"citations":0,"year":2024,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.739412568194049,"score":0.739412568194049,"has_metadata":true}]}